BT /F2 16 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (ORIGINAL DESIGN AND ON-DISK STRUCTURES) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (At the start of a FAT12 volume is a boot sector and BIOS Parameter Block \(BPB\). The BPB) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (records bytes per sector, sectors per cluster, number of reserved sectors, FAT copy count,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (root-entry capacity, media descriptor, sectors per FAT and total-sector count. The location) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (of each subsequent region is computed from these fields. A parser must reject impossible) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (and internally contradictory geometry rather than assume a familiar floppy layout.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (Each FAT12 entry is twelve bits. Consecutive entries are packed across byte boundaries; the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (usual byte offset for cluster n is floor\(3*n/2\). An even entry uses the low twelve bits of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (its two-byte window, an odd entry the high twelve. Entries encode free clusters, successor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (clusters, reserved and bad values, and end-of-chain markers. The two initial entries are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 512.0 Tm (reserved and the data region starts with cluster number two.) Tj ET
