BT /F2 16 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (ALLOCATION AND DIRECTORIES) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (The FAT is a chain table, not an allocation bitmap with extents. A file's first cluster is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (stored in its directory entry, and the FAT entry for that cluster points to the next) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (cluster until an end marker is reached. The design keeps file entries small but reading a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (badly fragmented file requires a chain walk and exposes many random metadata reads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (Duplicate ownership, cycles or a pointer outside the valid cluster range are corruption) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 592.0 Tm (indicators.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (The FAT12 root directory occupies a fixed region after the FAT copies; it is not a normal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (cluster chain. Subdirectories occupy clusters and contain entries including dot and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (dot-dot. Classic directory records are 32 bytes, with 8.3 names, attributes, timestamps,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 512.0 Tm (start-cluster and file length. VFAT long-name entries are a later compatibility layer and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 495.0 Tm (must be associated with the corresponding short entry using the prescribed ordering and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 478.0 Tm (checksum.) Tj ET
