BT /F2 16 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (DESIGN TRADE-OFFS AND HISTORICAL LIMITATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (Twelve-bit entries reduce metadata size for floppy capacities but cap the useful cluster) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (namespace. A fixed root-directory region imposes a separate directory-entry limit and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (prevents normal root growth. The linked allocation table scales poorly for large or heavily) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (fragmented files, and no permissions, resource forks, Unicode file names or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (crash-consistent transactions are part of the original DOS-era format.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (Compatibility often matters more than speed. A modern reader must tolerate legitimate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (legacy BPB variants while refusing ambiguous cluster geometry. The choice of cluster size) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (influences the maximum addressable data area and internal fragmentation. Metadata updates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (that span FAT copies, directory entries and user data are vulnerable to interruption.) Tj ET
